From 5fba8ad64875ff1aff6cd2ad111ca12c33fa6ba2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Prudhvi raj <prudhvirajkonda8@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:10:45 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] demos: fix sslecho receive buffer boundary handling

The rxbuf array in the sslecho, echecho, and dtlsecho demos was declared
as char rxbuf[128] with rxcap set to sizeof(rxbuf) (128).  SSL_read()
could return up to 128 bytes, and the subsequent null termination
rxbuf[rxlen] = 0 would then write one byte past the end of the buffer
at index 128.

This affected both the server-side and client-side receive paths in all
three demo programs.

Fix by declaring rxbuf with one extra byte (128 + 1 = 129) and setting
rxcap to sizeof(rxbuf) - 1 (128). This preserves the maximum 128-byte
read capacity while ensuring that the null terminator at rxbuf[128]
stays within bounds.

  [ dtlsecho and echecho do not exist on this branch, so the respective
    hunks are dropped. ]

Resolves: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/issues/33730
Fixes: ef6e427b4026 "DTLS 1.3 Demo and Bug Fix"
Fixes: 50580382caca "Documents initial agreed APIs for Encrypted Client Hello (ECH) and includes a minimal demo for some of those APIs."
Fixes: 801c638c5040 "Added Simple SSL Echo Client/Server to demos."
Reviewed-by: Matt Caswell <matt@openssl.foundation>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Fri Nov 20 17:51:06 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33747
(cherry picked from commit eb7d128d17dfa2dc7954b086348accec946bd21c)
---
 demos/sslecho/main.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/demos/sslecho/main.c b/demos/sslecho/main.c
index c954ce7ee07e..decede2443c2 100644
--- a/demos/sslecho/main.c
+++ b/demos/sslecho/main.c
@@ -148,8 +148,8 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
     char buffer[BUFFERSIZE];
     char *txbuf;
 
-    char rxbuf[128];
-    size_t rxcap = sizeof(rxbuf);
+    char rxbuf[128 + 1];
+    size_t rxcap = sizeof(rxbuf) - 1;
     int rxlen;
 
     char *rem_server_ip = NULL;
